gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.08570957596427853,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":74.3,"_gate_rev_durability":0.08565538829278418,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":67.8,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.014033032036027546,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":26.7,"_gate_share_shrink":0.008240795219190522,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":39.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.001772301460038822,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":97.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00234,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Reinsurance Group of America, Incorporated provides life and health, and asset-intensive reinsurance in the United States, Latin America, Canada, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, Asia, and Australia. It offers individual and group life and health, disability, long-term care, and critical illness reinsurance; and financial solutions, such as asset-intensive reinsurance, longevity reinsurance, stable value products, pension risk transfer transactions, and capital solutions. The company also provides reinsurance for mortality, morbidity, lapse, and investment-related risks; coinsurance of payout annuities; underwritten annuities; funding agreement backed note program and other capital motivated solutions; and superannuation. Reinsurance Group of America, Incorporated was founded in 1973 and is headquartered in Chesterfield, Missouri.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Tony  Cheng F.S.A. | President, CEO & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $5.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $5.5M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 7%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $887K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $10K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Reinsurance Group of America, I is a large-cap financial services business with a $17.1B market cap on $23.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $3.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 16 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.46\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.4%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 21% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.21673540668078506},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3678490.38},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 77% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 36% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","17 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Reinsurance Group (RGA) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/reinsurance-group-rga-q3-2026-214749000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794001957.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.077,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"RGA outlines 8% to 10% EPS growth target as it simplif